{
  "doc": "Lifted Verify commands and whether each is a shell comment (#2684): the first non-blank character is '#'. statusgen's shellCommentOnly and tools/desk/internal/verifycmd.CommentOnly are both held to this table; a command that is only a comment exits 0 with no output, so no executor may record it as a pass.",
  "vectors": [
    {"name": "inline heading", "cmd": "## Coverage", "commentOnly": true},
    {"name": "single hash word", "cmd": "#coverage", "commentOnly": true},
    {"name": "hash then space", "cmd": "# read the review", "commentOnly": true},
    {"name": "leading blanks", "cmd": "   \t## Coverage  ", "commentOnly": true},
    {"name": "shebang-shaped", "cmd": "#!/bin/sh", "commentOnly": true},
    {"name": "plain command", "cmd": "go test ./x -count=1", "commentOnly": false},
    {"name": "trailing comment", "cmd": "go test ./x -count=1 # the real check", "commentOnly": false},
    {"name": "quoted hash argument", "cmd": "grep -c '#' docs/x.md", "commentOnly": false},
    {"name": "hash mid-word", "cmd": "echo a#b", "commentOnly": false},
    {"name": "empty", "cmd": "", "commentOnly": false},
    {"name": "blank", "cmd": "   ", "commentOnly": false}
  ],
  "cellsDoc": "Whole Verify Command cells (#2684 review S1, F2; #3147): the cell-to-verdict mapping both modules are held to, not only the predicate. firstSpan is statusgen's lift of an unmarked cell (codeSpan; tools/desk's verifycmd ports it). marked: the cell carries an honoured cmd: span. lift: the command both modules execute (the marked command, else firstSpan), as the cell holds it; a GFM-escaped \\| is un-escaped only when the command runs (#1953), and the tools/desk executors run exactly that un-escaped string, never the whole cell (#3147). statusgen / desk: runs (executed), comment-refused (a shell comment, never executed, could-not-run) or refused (never executed, could-not-run: a prose mention, a blank lift, or a shell no-op such as `:` or a cmd.exe REM / :: remark). The two columns are equal on every cell: lift parity. passes: a runs cell exits 0 when run from an empty directory.",
  "cells": [
    {"name": "S1: inline heading span, then prose", "cell": "`## Coverage`: confirm every angle is answered", "firstSpan": "## Coverage", "marked": false, "lift": "## Coverage", "statusgen": "comment-refused", "desk": "comment-refused"},
    {"name": "S1: single-word comment span, then prose", "cell": "`#coverage`: present", "firstSpan": "#coverage", "marked": false, "lift": "#coverage", "statusgen": "comment-refused", "desk": "comment-refused"},
    {"name": "#2684: heading mention mid-prose", "cell": "Inspect the `## Coverage` section of the review and confirm every angle is addressed", "firstSpan": "## Coverage", "marked": false, "lift": "## Coverage", "statusgen": "comment-refused", "desk": "comment-refused"},
    {"name": "the whole cell is one comment span", "cell": "`## Coverage`", "firstSpan": "## Coverage", "marked": false, "lift": "## Coverage", "statusgen": "comment-refused", "desk": "comment-refused"},
    {"name": "bare cell, no code span", "cell": "# read the review", "firstSpan": "# read the review", "marked": false, "lift": "# read the review", "statusgen": "comment-refused", "desk": "comment-refused"},
